WEBVTT

00:00:02.370 --> 00:00:05.610
Honey, don't you feel bad for Sunao?

00:00:05.610 --> 00:00:06.990
Feel bad about what?

00:00:07.410 --> 00:00:10.860
I don't mind sending him to a rugby school...

00:00:11.780 --> 00:00:16.230
But let's wait until he's gotten himself 
settled in at grade school.

00:00:16.820 --> 00:00:19.620
Sunao's shy enough already.

00:00:20.170 --> 00:00:24.050
There are kids from Sunao's grade school
attending this school.

00:00:24.050 --> 00:00:28.500
He'll have friends in higher grades
by the day of the entrance ceremony.

00:00:28.500 --> 00:00:30.030
What's so wrong with that?

00:00:30.030 --> 00:00:31.050
Sheesh.

00:02:18.690 --> 00:02:20.490
Osaka Sunao-kun, huh?

00:02:19.010 --> 00:02:24.050
<b>Episode 19
 I'm Not Crying</b>

00:02:20.820 --> 00:02:23.680
You'll be starting as a first-year 
at Eno Grade School next spring?

00:02:23.680 --> 00:02:24.680
Nice to meet you.

00:02:25.230 --> 00:02:29.660
Is that the same school Renpei goes to? 
You're the same age, too.

00:02:29.660 --> 00:02:31.010
Renpei!

00:02:31.010 --> 00:02:32.170
"Renpei"?

00:02:32.780 --> 00:02:35.250
He's got a great feel for the game.

00:02:35.620 --> 00:02:39.130
He plays with the grade school students 
instead of the other preschoolers.

00:02:39.890 --> 00:02:40.890
Renpei!

00:02:47.480 --> 00:02:48.810
Renpei!

00:02:48.810 --> 00:02:49.480
Huh?

00:02:53.360 --> 00:02:54.500
What is it?

00:02:55.140 --> 00:02:56.710
This kid's joining us from today. He's—

00:02:56.710 --> 00:02:57.400
Suna!

00:02:57.400 --> 00:02:57.990
What?

00:02:58.700 --> 00:03:00.110
I'm Sunao.

00:03:00.110 --> 00:03:02.870
Renpei-kun, you're so cool!

00:03:02.870 --> 00:03:04.550
Let's be friends.

00:03:07.690 --> 00:03:13.140
<i>I've been followin' Renpei ever since.</i>

00:03:14.590 --> 00:03:16.170
<i>That's why I know how it goes.</i>

00:03:16.170 --> 00:03:20.970
<i>'Cause he's so good, everyone makes a fuss 
over him when he first joins a team, but...</i>

00:03:22.780 --> 00:03:25.590
You sure are insolent for a little kid.

00:03:25.590 --> 00:03:26.350
What?

00:03:26.350 --> 00:03:31.690
My insolence has nothin' to do
with your awful passes.

00:03:32.240 --> 00:03:35.170
Our team ain't gonna get any stronger 
with upperclassmen like you.

00:03:35.170 --> 00:03:37.370
I <i>know</i> you've been skippin' practice.

00:03:37.910 --> 00:03:39.230
What'd you say?!

00:03:39.230 --> 00:03:40.400
Renpei!

00:03:41.470 --> 00:03:44.760
<i>The same scenario'd play out even after 
we went into middle and high school.</i>

00:03:45.230 --> 00:03:47.950
<i>At first, everyone'd talk about 
their amazing new teammate</i>

00:03:47.950 --> 00:03:50.340
<i>and listen intently to Renpei,</i>

00:03:50.980 --> 00:03:53.430
<i>but they'd end up hatin' him 
'cause of his foul mouth.</i>

00:03:53.860 --> 00:03:55.460
<i>And once the team got stronger,</i>

00:03:55.980 --> 00:03:59.420
<i>everyone'd start treatin' Renpei
like a nuisance.</i>

00:04:02.140 --> 00:04:04.520
<i>I need to stand between them.</i>

00:04:05.890 --> 00:04:09.430
<b>Tenjiku</b>

00:04:05.890 --> 00:04:09.430
<b>Jinko</b>

00:04:06.560 --> 00:04:09.430
Let's go, Jinko!

00:04:11.930 --> 00:04:15.770
Guys, let's turn this around
one point at a time!

00:04:15.770 --> 00:04:17.190
Lemme hear you!

00:04:17.670 --> 00:04:19.320
Sunao...

00:04:19.320 --> 00:04:21.980
<i>It's not that Jinko's playin' well...</i>

00:04:21.980 --> 00:04:24.510
<i>We're just a little outta it right now.</i>

00:04:24.510 --> 00:04:26.930
<i>We'll be back to normal before long.</i>

00:04:28.350 --> 00:04:32.330
Sunao's shootin' his mouth off again.

00:04:33.470 --> 00:04:36.540
S'only a practice match. 
He's tryin' way too hard.

00:04:37.020 --> 00:04:38.750
He's so annoyin'.

00:04:39.700 --> 00:04:43.390
Well, shucks. The defense is too far forward.

00:04:43.390 --> 00:04:44.780
What are they? Idiots?

00:04:45.340 --> 00:04:47.180
No wonder they're gettin' past you.

00:04:49.260 --> 00:04:50.180
Those tackles are weak.

00:04:51.240 --> 00:04:54.150
Our forwards really are useless.

00:04:54.950 --> 00:04:58.190
What a stupid team.

00:04:59.150 --> 00:05:00.840
I hope you morons lose.

00:05:02.740 --> 00:05:06.340
Huh? Tenjiku's fullback is 
standing pretty far back.

00:05:06.340 --> 00:05:08.930
Huh? Oh, you're right.

00:05:08.930 --> 00:05:11.700
He was in the thick of it
up until a minute ago.

00:05:12.550 --> 00:05:16.330
Hey, now... Has Sakura Renpei
 thrown in the towel?

00:05:16.330 --> 00:05:20.280
From his standpoint at the back, 
the fullback can observe his entire team,

00:05:20.280 --> 00:05:22.440
and he's just standing there 
without issuing commands?

00:05:22.850 --> 00:05:25.920
He's probably thinking, 
"It's only a practice game."

00:05:28.300 --> 00:05:29.290
Renpei!

00:05:36.060 --> 00:05:38.850
Wow, what a halfhearted kick.

00:05:38.850 --> 00:05:41.570
He's completely demotivated.

00:05:55.470 --> 00:05:56.950
I don't care.

00:05:58.720 --> 00:06:02.670
I ain't playin' rugby to make friends.

00:06:03.360 --> 00:06:05.510
You shouldn't worry about me, either.

00:06:07.180 --> 00:06:10.230
I don't care, as long as the team wins.

00:06:16.300 --> 00:06:20.520
<i>I found that side of him really cool, too.</i>

00:06:25.300 --> 00:06:28.030
There he is. It's their substitute winger.

00:06:42.020 --> 00:06:43.710
Try!

00:06:43.710 --> 00:06:46.710
All right! It's 19-10!

00:06:46.710 --> 00:06:50.220
Kifune, make the kick!

00:06:51.280 --> 00:06:54.620
What's with your ugly mug?

00:06:58.360 --> 00:07:02.480
Why didn't you run?! 
You could've caught him!

00:07:03.430 --> 00:07:07.390
I don't feel like playin'. 
You guys do whatever you want.

00:07:07.390 --> 00:07:10.750
I don't care about this 
pointless game anymore.

00:07:13.560 --> 00:07:16.430
Renpei's not a bad guy.

00:07:17.430 --> 00:07:20.870
I don't care, as long as the team wins.

00:07:23.510 --> 00:07:27.460
Fine. Just stand there 
for the rest of your life.

00:07:31.130 --> 00:07:33.530
Actually, you'd just be in the way.

00:07:34.330 --> 00:07:36.640
Go back to the hotel or somethin'!

00:07:36.640 --> 00:07:39.730
That's the same, right?!
You ain't doing anythin' either way!

00:07:39.730 --> 00:07:41.640
Leave! Leave now!

00:07:48.950 --> 00:07:52.460
Renpei, you're the height of lame right now.

00:08:03.450 --> 00:08:04.430
Suna...

00:08:06.530 --> 00:08:08.920
Well said, Sunao.

00:08:08.920 --> 00:08:12.050
Renpei'll listen to you, for sure.

00:08:15.680 --> 00:08:19.060
You're all the same! Not a single
 one of you is tryin' to win!

00:08:19.060 --> 00:08:19.780
Sunao...

00:08:19.780 --> 00:08:22.920
You blame Renpei for everythin'
that goes wrong.

00:08:22.920 --> 00:08:26.810
There're fourteen of you. 
There ain't <i>no way </i>it's all his fault!

00:08:27.150 --> 00:08:30.870
We only have a month before 
the Hanazono preliminaries!

00:08:35.880 --> 00:08:42.110
I don't want to practice losin'
for another month.

00:08:42.830 --> 00:08:44.070
I want to win.

00:08:45.330 --> 00:08:52.090
Even if you guys don't care, 
I'm gonna try an' win.

00:08:54.590 --> 00:08:58.600
We made the kick! It's 21-10.

00:09:04.530 --> 00:09:06.270
All right!

00:09:05.270 --> 00:09:06.270
Let's go!

00:09:07.120 --> 00:09:09.020
<i>I'll win. I'm gonna win.</i>

00:09:13.000 --> 00:09:16.860
<i>Everyone on our team 
does whatever they want.</i>

00:09:20.310 --> 00:09:22.620
<i>Our team lacks tradition. 
We lack cohesion.</i>

00:09:23.190 --> 00:09:24.960
<i>All we ever do is fight.</i>

00:09:26.140 --> 00:09:29.520
<i>But after bein' on this team for three 
years, I can't start hatin' them all now.</i>

00:09:30.630 --> 00:09:33.880
<i>I wanna win everythin' at this training 
camp, ride the wings of success,</i>

00:09:34.320 --> 00:09:38.890
<i>and go to the Hanazono prelims
with these guys.</i>

00:09:42.690 --> 00:09:45.030
<i>I wanna go to Hanazono.</i>

00:10:00.970 --> 00:10:02.040
Are you okay?

00:10:02.660 --> 00:10:03.620
Can you stand?

00:10:15.880 --> 00:10:17.770
Th-Thanks...

00:10:22.060 --> 00:10:24.970
Knock-on by Jinko! Scrum, Tenjiku's ball.

00:10:24.970 --> 00:10:26.330
Don't worry about it!

00:10:26.330 --> 00:10:28.640
Jinko, you'll get the ball back!

00:10:36.860 --> 00:10:41.450
<i>Just one. We can start... with one tr—</i>

00:10:45.070 --> 00:10:46.080
Sunao!

00:10:47.870 --> 00:10:49.870
<i>I can't do it.</i>

00:10:52.430 --> 00:10:55.090
<i>We can't win.</i>

00:11:03.780 --> 00:11:05.290
You ain't goin' anywhere.

00:11:07.020 --> 00:11:09.350
Sunao, get the ball out.

00:11:12.250 --> 00:11:13.890
Go! Go!

00:11:15.070 --> 00:11:18.030
Sunao-san, I'm sorry.

00:11:18.030 --> 00:11:22.720
Somewhere in my heart,
I figured there's always next year.

00:11:22.720 --> 00:11:23.870
But there isn't.

00:11:23.870 --> 00:11:24.820
Sekki...

00:11:24.820 --> 00:11:26.700
This roster only exists this year!

00:11:27.440 --> 00:11:31.420
I wanna go to Hanazono with this team, too!

00:11:41.170 --> 00:11:44.050
Tenjiku's collective body 
language has changed.

00:11:44.050 --> 00:11:46.140
Their passes are connecting.

00:11:46.590 --> 00:11:50.770
Is it because of the argument 
between #13 and Sakura Renpei?

00:11:51.530 --> 00:11:53.520
I wonder what they were talking about.

00:11:55.020 --> 00:11:58.780
They're 22 meters inside Jinko's territory!

00:12:04.920 --> 00:12:09.390
Sunao, you okay? You hurt anywhere?

00:12:09.390 --> 00:12:14.460
Hikaru, I'm fine. Their captain's a good guy.

00:12:14.460 --> 00:12:15.670
Yeah.

00:12:16.050 --> 00:12:18.900
This isn't good! Don't let them 
push any further forward!

00:12:19.710 --> 00:12:21.930
And we were on a roll, too...

00:12:21.930 --> 00:12:24.380
Jinko, stand strong!

00:12:28.440 --> 00:12:30.350
Those lightning passes!

00:12:30.350 --> 00:12:31.220
That spells bad news.

00:12:31.610 --> 00:12:36.980
Jinko's defense is all clumped together
because they're so close to goal.

00:12:39.210 --> 00:12:41.950
Their #14, Oshima, is on the extreme outside.

00:12:41.950 --> 00:12:42.930
Will they catch him?

00:12:45.850 --> 00:12:46.990
Ebucchi!

00:12:50.540 --> 00:12:53.000
You're light as a feather!

00:12:59.500 --> 00:13:00.930
Try!

00:13:01.510 --> 00:13:04.010
All right!

00:13:04.480 --> 00:13:08.070
I did it! I regained my dishonor!

00:13:06.960 --> 00:13:09.930
Ukyo-san, you mean you redeemed 
yourself <i>from </i>your dishonor.

00:13:09.930 --> 00:13:12.900
All right! Good job, Ukyo!

00:13:12.900 --> 00:13:14.280
Hikaru!

00:13:14.280 --> 00:13:17.440
Apparently, "regainin' your dishonor" 
is a phrase that's gettin' popular nowadays.

00:13:17.440 --> 00:13:19.020
What? Really?

00:13:17.710 --> 00:13:20.540
You did good. You did good, Ukyo.

00:13:20.540 --> 00:13:22.030
I'm so happy.

00:13:22.030 --> 00:13:26.030
I get that you're happy, but how 
 long're you gonna keep huggin' me?

00:13:26.030 --> 00:13:27.380
Forever.

00:13:29.530 --> 00:13:31.540
21-15.

00:13:31.540 --> 00:13:35.540
If they make this kick, they'll only need
 one more try to turn the game on its head.

00:13:35.540 --> 00:13:37.830
They've got just over 
ten minutes left, right?

00:13:37.830 --> 00:13:40.330
Th-This can't be good...

00:13:41.930 --> 00:13:43.260
Hey.

00:13:44.260 --> 00:13:47.570
Do you want to play, Oharano?

00:13:51.060 --> 00:13:52.120
Not really.

00:13:54.620 --> 00:13:57.020
<b>Who are you
 calling "the substitute winger"?</b>

00:13:57.020 --> 00:14:00.020
<b>SQUEEEEEZE</b>

00:13:57.910 --> 00:14:00.020
<b>Argh!</b>

00:14:02.330 --> 00:14:03.490
Sorry!

00:14:03.490 --> 00:14:07.250
Don't sweat it, Toru. I left you 
in a bad position to kick from.

00:14:09.900 --> 00:14:10.870
Matsuo.

00:14:14.080 --> 00:14:19.070
We're switching fly-halves 
from Matsuo to Oharano.

00:14:20.350 --> 00:14:21.900
It's Oharano-kun!

00:14:21.900 --> 00:14:23.340
Aren't you lucky?

00:14:23.340 --> 00:14:26.590
We might lose the lead from here.
Keep us in it.

00:14:26.590 --> 00:14:28.970
Hey, Oharano!

00:14:29.500 --> 00:14:33.850
What did you think of my 
flank play, huh? Well?

00:14:35.070 --> 00:14:36.530
Absolutely terrible.

00:14:38.480 --> 00:14:40.860
You need to run at least 
a hundred times harder.

00:14:40.860 --> 00:14:44.180
What? Your demands are way too extreme.

00:14:44.180 --> 00:14:47.790
But I could probably go ten...
no, five times harder...

00:14:47.790 --> 00:14:49.240
Hey, you little turd.

00:14:49.620 --> 00:14:52.260
You think <i>you </i>can replace Matsu-san?

00:14:52.260 --> 00:14:55.240
You've been sulking on the sidelines
for weeks now.

00:14:55.240 --> 00:14:58.000
Are you even fit enough to move?

00:14:59.250 --> 00:15:03.270
Ebumi-senpai, I'll admit you're fast.

00:15:03.270 --> 00:15:05.410
I hope you'll follow my instructions.

00:15:05.410 --> 00:15:06.250
What?!

00:15:06.250 --> 00:15:08.460
Good work, Matsu-san.

00:15:06.640 --> 00:15:08.250
You can't be serious!

00:15:08.250 --> 00:15:09.640
I'll hear you out after the game.

00:15:08.460 --> 00:15:09.640
Thanks.

00:15:09.640 --> 00:15:11.240
I'll make sure you never hear again!

00:15:09.640 --> 00:15:11.460
They're already fighting.

00:15:11.240 --> 00:15:12.760
Just shut up and listen.

00:15:11.460 --> 00:15:12.760
Yeah, sounds like it.

00:15:12.760 --> 00:15:16.040
You guys get along terribly.

00:15:16.040 --> 00:15:18.260
What was that, you stupid little midget?

00:15:18.780 --> 00:15:19.910
Hey, stupid midget, come here.

00:15:19.910 --> 00:15:20.890
What did you call me?!

00:15:27.280 --> 00:15:29.100
We'll score another try!

00:15:29.960 --> 00:15:31.410
Run!

00:15:34.180 --> 00:15:36.360
Tenjiku's on a roll.

00:15:36.360 --> 00:15:40.500
Once you make one good play, 
they keep on coming.

00:15:43.300 --> 00:15:46.590
No way! They're already 
22 meters into our half.

00:15:46.930 --> 00:15:49.200
Jinko, hang in there!

00:15:49.630 --> 00:15:51.780
<i>We can do it. This is goin' well.</i>

00:15:56.470 --> 00:15:57.140
Gion!

00:15:59.410 --> 00:16:02.230
You can ignore Tenjiku's forwards.

00:16:02.570 --> 00:16:06.230
If the ball is passed to the backs,
 rush forward to meet them.

00:16:06.780 --> 00:16:09.230
I don't have to stop the forwards?

00:16:09.230 --> 00:16:13.150
Nope. Since you never seem to stop 
moving, you should be able to handle it.

00:16:13.550 --> 00:16:14.530
We're counting on you.

00:16:15.790 --> 00:16:19.430
<i>He's fast, but I just have
 to pass it back inside...</i>

00:16:23.010 --> 00:16:24.920
An interception!

00:16:39.390 --> 00:16:41.640
That son of a bitch first-year!

00:16:41.640 --> 00:16:43.890
Oh, nice catch.

00:16:43.890 --> 00:16:46.150
How dare he order me around?! 
Later, I'm going to kill—

00:16:50.780 --> 00:16:53.110
A dangerous high tackle! Penalty!

00:16:53.110 --> 00:16:56.070
Ow!

00:16:56.070 --> 00:16:57.120
Sorry! Sorry!

00:16:57.120 --> 00:17:00.740
Seriously? I expected more from you.
He caught up to you.

00:17:00.740 --> 00:17:01.780
What?!

00:17:01.780 --> 00:17:02.940
Oharano.

00:17:02.940 --> 00:17:03.370
Huh?

00:17:03.370 --> 00:17:06.030
I rushed forward, just like you said.

00:17:06.030 --> 00:17:07.760
Oh, yeah. Not bad.

00:17:07.760 --> 00:17:08.670
"Not bad"?

00:17:08.670 --> 00:17:10.610
Time for your next instructions.

00:17:10.610 --> 00:17:13.170
You really know how to get on one's nerves.

00:17:13.170 --> 00:17:14.870
Iwashimizu-kun, come here.

00:17:14.870 --> 00:17:16.760
Huh? Okay.

00:17:17.410 --> 00:17:20.320
Looks like they're getting along.

00:17:24.930 --> 00:17:26.530
A line-out?

00:17:26.530 --> 00:17:29.420
They're ten meters from the goal line.

00:17:30.420 --> 00:17:32.030
Come on, Jinko.

00:17:32.480 --> 00:17:34.410
We're counting on you.

00:17:34.410 --> 00:17:35.320
Okay.

00:17:43.740 --> 00:17:45.910
Hachi-senpai!

00:17:45.910 --> 00:17:47.250
Over here!

00:17:47.250 --> 00:17:49.250
Throw me a long whatever-it-is my way!

00:17:49.770 --> 00:17:51.250
Over here!

00:17:51.250 --> 00:17:53.760
G-Gion, what are you—

00:17:51.250 --> 00:17:55.150
Hachi-senpai, over here!

00:17:55.150 --> 00:17:57.360
Hey, over here!

00:18:05.980 --> 00:18:08.040
The little guy was a decoy.

00:18:13.150 --> 00:18:14.860
Push Iwashimizu!

00:18:15.210 --> 00:18:17.320
It's a maul!

00:18:17.320 --> 00:18:18.860
Push, Jinko!

00:18:25.450 --> 00:18:27.120
Hang in there, Iwashimizu!

00:18:27.530 --> 00:18:30.880
You're the core! You can't break!

00:18:31.240 --> 00:18:33.000
Y-Yes, sir.

00:18:34.230 --> 00:18:35.810
Ise-senpai, get in the maul!

00:18:35.810 --> 00:18:36.460
What?

00:18:36.460 --> 00:18:39.200
Don't worry about your position. Just push.

00:18:39.200 --> 00:18:39.970
Push!

00:18:46.490 --> 00:18:48.070
Gion-kun, the ball!

00:18:50.520 --> 00:18:51.910
Get the ball!

00:18:55.340 --> 00:18:57.860
All right, Gion! Let's push!

00:18:58.430 --> 00:18:59.430
Yeah!

00:19:00.450 --> 00:19:03.450
Everyone, get in here!

00:19:05.020 --> 00:19:07.750
Stand strong, dammit!

00:19:10.960 --> 00:19:12.590
{A: split this "Push" out as it sounded like someone else was saying it}Push!

00:19:12.590 --> 00:19:13.960
Push, Jinko!

00:19:17.080 --> 00:19:18.750
Five meters left!

00:19:19.470 --> 00:19:21.470
Push!

00:20:00.130 --> 00:20:02.380
Gion-kun, get it down!

00:20:03.200 --> 00:20:04.890
Score the try!

00:20:04.890 --> 00:20:06.500
Hurry!

00:20:20.920 --> 00:20:22.500
Try!

00:20:23.910 --> 00:20:26.570
You did it, Gion!

00:20:26.570 --> 00:20:28.000
Gion!

00:20:28.000 --> 00:20:29.540
Gion!

00:20:29.110 --> 00:20:33.410
Way to go!

00:20:29.540 --> 00:20:31.570
Nice try!

00:20:33.410 --> 00:20:35.640
All right, Gion!

00:20:35.640 --> 00:20:37.520
It's 26-16.

00:20:38.090 --> 00:20:40.420
Oh, jeez. I'm going to cry...

00:20:44.430 --> 00:20:47.720
There's no time for that. 
You're in the way of the conversion.

00:20:47.720 --> 00:20:48.990
Get back to your positions.

00:20:49.650 --> 00:20:51.560
Kifune-senpai, you're kicking, right?

00:20:52.130 --> 00:20:55.560
We'll score one more and finish 
them off. Hurry up and—

00:21:09.210 --> 00:21:12.680
What are you crying for? We haven't won yet!

00:21:13.320 --> 00:21:16.670
I-I'm not crying!

00:21:16.670 --> 00:21:18.680
Hurry up, idiot!

00:21:18.680 --> 00:21:20.540
I'm going, idiot!

00:21:22.610 --> 00:21:24.390
That's a difficult angle.

00:21:24.390 --> 00:21:25.810
Can he make it?

00:21:33.310 --> 00:21:35.100
Kifune!

00:21:35.100 --> 00:21:36.260
Awesome...

00:21:36.260 --> 00:21:38.310
28-15!

00:21:38.930 --> 00:21:41.090
It ain't over yet!

00:21:48.570 --> 00:21:49.880
Nice, Hosoyan!

00:21:49.880 --> 00:21:50.700
Hurry!

00:21:52.970 --> 00:21:54.520
Just two more tries!

00:21:54.520 --> 00:21:56.960
Two more tries, and we'll have the lead!

00:23:44.980 --> 00:23:49.990
<b>Next Time: "Aren't You Happy?"</b>

00:23:46.240 --> 00:23:49.160
Next Time: "Aren't You Happy?"
